    'Data residency requirements are a particular concern for biometric data. Several African countries require that biometric data be stored within national borders, which has implications for organizations using cloud-based verification services.',
    'For organizations deploying biometric verification, integration architecture matters significantly. Best practice involves edge-processing selfies on the device where possible to minimize data transmission, using encrypted channels for all biometric data flows, and implementing tokenized identity references so that raw biometric templates are never stored in application databases.',
    'Looking ahead, the integration of biometric verification with national identity systems is expected to accelerate. Several African governments are developing digital identity infrastructure that will enable real-time biometric verification against authoritative government databases.',
